* ATmega32/ATmega32L Pin Definitions -- 40-pin PDIP and 44-lead
* TQFP/44-pad QFN/MLF packages (combined)
* Source: Atmel 2503Q-AVR-02/11 "ATmega32(L) Datasheet", Figure 1
* (Pinout, PDIP and TQFP/MLF views) and the Pin Descriptions section.
*
* Companion devices -- ATmega32 and ATmega32L differ only in
* operating voltage range (2.7V-5.5V for L vs. 4.5V-5.5V for
* non-L) and maximum speed grade (8MHz vs. 16MHz). Same silicon,
* same 32 I/O lines, same pin functions -- genuinely pin-compatible,
* not merely package variants of a memory-size family like the
* ATmega328 case. Both included:
*   ATmega32, ATmega32L
*
* NOT included -- ATmega32U4, despite the similar part number, is a
* distinct device (adds a full-speed USB controller, different I/O
* line count, different package). Not pin-compatible with this
* family; already has its own separate .qpindef file from a prior
* session.
*
* Package scope -- 40-pin PDIP and 44-pin TQFP/QFN/MLF are combined
* into this single file. The 44-pin package's four extra physical
* pins vs. the 40-pin package are ALL duplicate VCC/GND pins for
* power distribution (VCC: x1 on PDIP vs. x3 on TQFP/MLF; GND: x2 on
* PDIP vs. x4 on TQFP/MLF) -- not additional signals, not NC pins.
* Every other signal (32 GPIO pins across PORTA-D, RESET, XTAL1,
* XTAL2, AREF, AVCC) appears exactly once on both packages. Per this
* project's established handling, multiple physical VCC/GND pins
* collapse to a single V/G record regardless of package, so the two
* packages are fully combinable here. The QFN/MLF variant additionally
* has an exposed thermal pad that should be soldered to ground -- not
* a distinct signal, already covered by the G record.
*
* Pin classifications:
*   PA0-PA7 -- Port A, bidirectional GPIO; ADC0-ADC7 alternate
*              function (8-channel 10-bit ADC, single-ended; 7 of
*              these channels also serve differential/gain-amplified
*              inputs in the TQFP package per the datasheet, not a
*              pin-count-affecting distinction). Classified B.
*   PB0-PB7 -- Port B, bidirectional GPIO; alternate functions XCK/T0,
*              T1, INT2/AIN0, OC0/AIN1, SS, MOSI, MISO, SCK (SPI +
*              Timer/Counter + Analog Comparator + external interrupt
*              muxing). Classified B.
*   PC0-PC7 -- Port C, bidirectional GPIO; alternate functions SCL,
*              SDA (TWI), TCK/TMS/TDO/TDI (JTAG -- datasheet notes
*              "When the JTAG interface is enabled, this pin can not
*              be used as an I/O pin" for PC2-PC5, a fuse/register-
*              gated restriction, not a change to the pin's
*              fundamental B classification), TOSC1/TOSC2 (Timer2
*              async oscillator). Classified B.
*   PD0-PD7 -- Port D, bidirectional GPIO; alternate functions RXD,
*              TXD (USART), INT0, INT1, OC1B, OC1A, ICP1, OC2.
*              Classified B.
*   RESET    -- Dedicated active-low Reset input. Unlike newer AVR
*              parts (e.g. ATmega328P), this datasheet documents no
*              RSTDISBL fuse -- RESET is never GPIO-capable on this
*              device. Classified I.
*   XTAL1    -- "Input to the inverting Oscillator amplifier and
*              input to the internal clock operating circuit."
*              Dedicated pin, not shared with any GPIO port (unlike
*              newer AVR parts where XTAL1/2 double with PB6/PB7).
*              Classified I.
*   XTAL2    -- "Output from the inverting Oscillator amplifier."
*              Dedicated, not GPIO-shared. Classified O.
*   AVCC     -- Separate analog supply pin for Port A and the ADC.
*              Datasheet: "It should be externally connected to VCC,
*              even if the ADC is not used." Recorded as I per this
*              project's established workaround for AVCC-style pins.
*   AREF     -- External ADC voltage reference input; dedicated, not
*              multiplexed with any GPIO port bit.

D ATmega32/ATmega32L 40-Pin PDIP / 44-Pin TQFP/QFN/MLF 8-bit AVR Microcontroller
P ATmega32 ATmega32L

V VCC
I AREF
I AVCC
B PA0 ADC0
B PA1 ADC1
B PA2 ADC2
B PA3 ADC3
B PA4 ADC4
B PA5 ADC5
B PA6 ADC6
B PA7 ADC7
B PB0 XCK/T0
B PB1 T1
B PB2 INT2/AIN0
B PB3 OC0/AIN1
B PB4 SS
B PB5 MOSI
B PB6 MISO
B PB7 SCK
K SIMCLK

B PC0 SCL
B PC1 SDA
B PC2 TCK
B PC3 TMS
B PC4 TDO
B PC5 TDI
B PC6 TOSC1
B PC7 TOSC2
B PD0 RXD
B PD1 TXD
B PD2 INT0
B PD3 INT1
B PD4 OC1B
B PD5 OC1A
B PD6 ICP1
B PD7 OC2
I RESET
I XTAL1
O XTAL2
G GND
